{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on environment and air quality monitoring for Environment : Tumakuru, covering the city of Tumakuru, Karnataka. It provides monthly mean concentrations of key air pollutants such as PM2.5, PM10, NO2, SO2, and O3, derived from sensor-based observations. These indicators support smart city air-quality tracking, local environmental assessment, and evidence-based planning for reducing residential air pollution. Published under the Smart Cities Mission with involvement of the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs and the Karnataka and Tumakuru administrations.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Residential Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together environment-focused information for Ujjain, Madhya Pradesh, supporting local planning and monitoring under the Smart Cities Mission. It covers sanitation-related aspects alongside broader environmental themes, enabling stakeholders to assess conditions and prioritize improvements in urban services. Published by the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs with Smart Cities Mission partners, the resources are intended for city-level decision-making and program tracking for Ujjain.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Sanitation"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on urban air quality in Environment : Varanasi, covering monthly mean concentrations of key pollutants including PM2.5, PM10, NO2, SO2 and O3. Data is generated through city air-quality monitoring/sensors to support tracking pollution levels and understanding temporal variations for local planning and public health awareness. It is published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, with involvement from Uttar Pradesh and Varanasi.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Residential Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers environment advance pollutants in Chandigarh, focusing on key air quality indicators such as NH3, O3, PM2.5 and PM10. It also includes related pollutant measures reported for Chandigarh, supporting monitoring and assessment of urban air pollution trends. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission and Chandigarh, the resources are useful for researchers, planners and city administrators working on pollution control and compliance-oriented analysis.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Vehicular Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on environment air quality in Chandigarh, covering key pollutants such as CO, NO, NOX, and NH3. It supports monitoring and analysis of vehicular air pollution patterns to inform urban air-quality management and public health-oriented interventions. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs, aligned with the Smart Cities Mission and Chandigarh, the resources are suited for researchers, planners, and city administrators tracking air quality trends and compliance needs.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Vehicular Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers environment pollutants—NO, NOX, Benzene, Toluene, Oxylene, WS, RH, SR and RG—measured for Chandigarh. It supports understanding of air quality and pollutant patterns relevant to urban environmental monitoring and planning. The datasets are published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs, aligned with the Smart Cities Mission and Chandigarh initiatives, and can be used for analysis of vehicular air pollution impacts and related mitigation efforts.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Vehicular Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Environmental : Jammu catalog brings together 2018 city-level air quality information for Jammu, focusing on pollution levels measured through monitoring/sensor-based observations. It covers monthly mean concentrations of key pollutants including PM2.5, PM10, NO2, SO2, and O3, supporting analysis of temporal trends and assessment of air quality conditions. The catalog is aligned with urban environmental monitoring under the Smart Cities Mission, enabling researchers, planners, and citizens to track pollutant behavior for the City of Jammu during 2018.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Industrial Air Pollution, Environment and Forest; Vehicular Air Pollution, Environment and Forest; Residential Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers environmental clearance granted through PARIVESH 2.0, a role-based workflow system used for online submission and monitoring of proposals seeking Environment, Forest, Wildlife and CRZ clearances. It supports tracking of proposals across workflow stages, including submission, updates, and status visibility for relevant authorities and proponents. Published by the Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change, the resources apply across India and are intended to help stakeholders verify clearance outcomes and follow proposal processing over time.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides environmental information for the City of Jhansi, focusing on urban air pollution monitoring. It covers monthly mean concentrations of key pollutants including PM2.5, PM10, NO2, SO2 and O3, supporting trend analysis and local assessment of air quality. The data is published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, with relevance for city-level planning and public health awareness in Jhansi.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Industrial Air Pollution"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together equipment-related information from the Livestock Census for rural and urban areas across India. It focuses on implements and machinery used for livestock rearing, including mechanized tools such as choppers, balers, cutters, and milking equipment, along with related disposal and dung-handling machinery. Published by the Department of Animal Husbandry and Dairying and the Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying, the series supports planning, monitoring, and analysis of livestock-sector mechanization over the census cycle.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Animal Husbandry"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides equivalent green weight estimates at country level, broken down by age and soundness, expressed in '000 tonnes. Sourced from the India State of Forest Report 2011, the indicators support analysis of forest biomass characteristics across age classes and soundness categories. These data can be used for planning, monitoring, and reporting related to forest resources and their condition. The coverage is for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest Resources"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides error matrix information for forest-related classification outputs, supporting assessment of classification accuracy against reference/ground truth. It is useful for evaluating how well mapped forest classes align with observed conditions, including categories such as dense, moderately dense, and open forest, and for reporting accuracy measures derived from the matrix. Published by NITI Aayog, the resources cover India-wide results for forest mapping and related analytics.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together statistics on estimated average daily employment and the number of working factories in India. It covers employment of persons engaged directly or through agencies in manufacturing processes and related incidental work, including attendance-based measures used to derive average daily employment. These indicators support analysis of factory-level labour absorption, industrial workforce trends, and monitoring of employment conditions in the manufacturing sector. The data are published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation.",
  "generated_sector": "Labour and Employment; Employment"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides estimated average factory employment in working factories across India, broken down by states at the 2-digit level of NIC-2004 and NIC-2008. It covers employment measures linked to working factories and industry activities, supporting analysis of labour demand and industrial structure by state and industry classification. These estimates are useful for researchers, planners, and policymakers tracking employment trends in manufacturing and related activities. The data is published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation for the years 2004 and 2008.",
  "generated_sector": "Labour and Employment; Employment"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together estimates of employment across the public and private sectors in India, with breakdowns by Central Government, State Government, quasi-government bodies, and local bodies. It also covers private sector employment by larger and smaller establishments. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, these statistics support labour market analysis, policy planning, and monitoring of employment trends across institutional sectors.",
  "generated_sector": "Labour and Employment; Employment"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together estimates of the number of species across various taxonomic groups, supporting comparative analysis of biodiversity by group. It covers taxonomic categories such as Protista, Animalia, Arthropoda and Chordata, with an environment and forest focus. These estimates are useful for researchers, planners and policy analysts who need group-wise biodiversity indicators for India. The data are published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest Resources"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together estimates of postal traffic in India, covering the estimated number of postcards, letters, newspapers, parcels and packets handled. It spans 2000-01 to 2010-11, supporting analysis of trends in mail and parcel movement over time. The statistics are useful for planning and monitoring postal service demand and operational workload. Published under the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the collection supports evidence-based reporting and research in information and communications.",
  "generated_sector": "Information and Communications; Post"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together region-wise and state-wise estimates of the wild elephant population across India. It covers the period 2002 onwards, supporting trend analysis and monitoring of elephant populations over time. The estimates are useful for wildlife planning, conservation prioritization, and policy review by enabling comparisons across regions and states. The data is published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest Resources"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers estimated proportions of supplementary nutrition funds spent on children in India, focusing on how much of total supplementary nutrition expenditure is directed to children and how delivery estimates relate to actual spending. It provides state-wise breakdowns for 2008-09, including children’s supplementary nutrition expenditure as a percentage of total supplementary nutrition expenditure and the estimated value delivered to children as a percentage of actual expenditure. The insights support monitoring and planning of child nutrition and related Anganwadi services. Published by NITI Aayog.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together estimates of additional vessels and the associated investment requirements for India’s shipping sector. It supports planning and policy analysis for capacity expansion, procurement prioritization, and investment decision-making. The datasets are published by NITI Aayog and focus on shipping and vessel-related requirements, providing an overview suitable for government stakeholders and researchers assessing maritime transport growth.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Water ways"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together statistics on the estimated reserve and installed capacity of various sources of energies in India. It covers key energy types such as coal, crude, gas, lignite, and oil, along with electricity and renewable energy capacity indicators. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the datasets support energy planning, monitoring of supply potential, and analysis of capacity trends across conventional and renewable sources.",
  "generated_sector": "Power and Energy; Renewable"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides estimated state-wise enrolment in various social categories, covering All categories, Scheduled Caste, Scheduled Tribe, and Other Backward Classes. It includes breakdowns by gender, with estimates for male and female students. These indicators support monitoring participation and equity in higher education planning and policy analysis. The estimates are for India and are published by the Ministry of Education, Department of Higher Education.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides estimates of the stock of engineering degree holders in the working age group by selected disciplines for India. Using inputs from the National Technical Manpower Information System (NTMIS) and AICTE, it supports analysis of higher education and workforce supply trends across engineering specializations. The series is available from 1994 onwards, enabling researchers and policymakers to study discipline-wise development and inform planning for science, technology and research-related human resources. Published under the Ministry of Science and Technology/Department of Science and Technology (DST) and NSTMIS.",
  "generated_sector": "Science and Technology; Research & Development"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together estimates of the stock of Science and Technology personnel, compiled from the Institute of Applied Manpower Research (IAMR), New Delhi. It supports analysis of human resources for science and technology and can be used for planning, monitoring and policy discussions around research and development capacity. Published by the Ministry of Science and Technology, Department of Science and Technology (DST) and the National Science and Technology Management Information System (NSTMIS), the coverage is for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Science and Technology; Research & Development"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides estimated average available funds for Supplementary Nutrition for different types of beneficiaries, expressed per beneficiary per day in rupees. It covers the 2008-09 period and supports analysis of how allocations for supplementary nutrition are distributed across beneficiary categories, including child-focused services linked to Anganwadi/AWC. The estimates help assess programme funding against norms and identify gaps in state-level availability. Published by NITI Aayog for use in nutrition programme monitoring and planning across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog presents estimated effective coverage in the Supplementary Nutrition Programme (SNP) for children under ICDS across India. It focuses on coverage gaps—survey gap, service gap, and delivery gap—along with actual coverage measures using survey number, delivery number, and estimated total eligible children. These indicators support planning and monitoring of nutrition service delivery for children, helping NITI Aayog and stakeholders identify where coverage shortfalls occur and target improvements.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides estimated enrolment in colleges across India, covering both state-level and all-India estimates. It presents gender-wise estimated enrolment for undergraduate and postgraduate programmes, supporting analysis of participation trends in higher education. The estimates are produced using a sampling approach with programme levels used as strata to ensure sufficient representation. Published by the Ministry of Education, Department of Higher Education, the data can be used for planning, monitoring, and policy evaluation in college education.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Estimates of the number of workers across India are presented for different States/UTs, covering unincorporated non-agricultural activities across sectors. The tables break down workers by sector and enterprise type and include percentage shares to support comparisons and ranking. These statistics help in understanding employment patterns in unorganized settings and can be used for planning, monitoring, and policy analysis by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation.",
  "generated_sector": "Labour and Employment; Unorganized Sector Workers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together estimates of the number of enterprises across India, covering unincorporated non-agricultural enterprises in different States/UTs. It supports analysis of enterprise distribution and relative shares across regions, with rankings based on descending order of enterprise counts. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the tables are useful for planning, monitoring economic activity, and informing research on rural and urban enterprise patterns.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Statistics"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together estimates of the number of manufacturing enterprises across India, covering different States/UTs. It focuses on unincorporated non-agricultural manufacturing enterprises and supports analysis of enterprise distribution and relative shares across locations. The statistics are useful for planning, industrial profiling, and evidence-based policy discussions on manufacturing activity. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the coverage spans India and its States/UTs.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Statistics"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together estimates of the number of unincorporated non-agricultural other service enterprises across India, with supporting percentage shares for comparative analysis. It is intended to support planning and policy discussions on the size and distribution of service enterprise activity across States/UTs. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the tables help users examine enterprise presence and relative shares by geography for evidence-based decision-making.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Statistics"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together estimates of the number of persons in India (in millions) derived from NSS 61st and 66th Round. It supports analysis of labour and employment status by covering rural and urban areas and distinguishing persons by labour force/workforce/unemployed categories. These indicators are useful for understanding employment conditions and for planning and monitoring labour market policies. The data are published by NITI Aayog and focus on India.",
  "generated_sector": "Labour and Employment; Employment"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides estimates of the number of stems by species and diameter class in Trees Outside Forest (TOF) at country level, reported in thousands. It is sourced from the India State of Forest Report 2011 and supports analysis of tree composition and size-class distribution beyond forest areas. These indicators are useful for forestry planning, biodiversity and vegetation assessments, and monitoring changes in TOF resources over time. The data cover India.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest Resources"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together estimates of the number of trading enterprises across India, covering unincorporated non-agricultural trading enterprises by State/UT. It supports analysis of enterprise distribution and relative shares across regions, useful for planning, monitoring, and research on trade-related economic activity. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the tables enable comparisons between rural and urban contexts where available within the underlying resources.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Statistics"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Estimates of the number of workers in the manufacturing sector across India are provided for different States/UTs, broken down by sector and enterprise type. The tables cover workers in unincorporated non-agricultural manufacturing activities and include percentage shares for combined enterprises, with rankings based on descending values. These statistics support analysis of employment patterns in manufacturing, including distinctions between rural and urban contexts and enterprise structures. The data are published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation.",
  "generated_sector": "Labour and Employment; Unorganized Sector Workers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Estimates of the number of workers in the other services sector are compiled for different States/UTs in India, covering unincorporated non-agricultural activities by sector and enterprise type. The tables also provide percentage shares across combined enterprises and rank States/UTs based on these shares. These statistics support labour market analysis, planning, and policy discussions on employment in unorganized services. The data are published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation.",
  "generated_sector": "Labour and Employment; Unorganized Sector Workers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Estimates of the number of workers in the trading sector are provided for different States/UTs in India, covering unincorporated non-agricultural enterprises. The tables present worker counts by sector and enterprise type, along with percentage shares across all enterprises in the combined sector, ranked by decreasing share. These statistics support labour market analysis and planning for employment in unorganized trading activities. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation.",
  "generated_sector": "Labour and Employment; Unorganized Sector Workers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Estimates of Tree and Mangrove Cover provides time-series information on forest cover, focusing on tree cover and mangrove cover. It covers India-wide estimates from 2001 onwards and state-wise estimates from 2007 onwards, aligned to the All India geographical area. The series supports monitoring of environmental change, planning for conservation and coastal ecosystem management, and evidence-based reporting. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, it is useful for researchers, policymakers, and analysts tracking land cover dynamics.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest Resources"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Estimates of Urban Transport Investments by High Powered Expert Committee (HPEC) compile investment requirements for urban transport and related infrastructure services for India. Prepared under the HPEC chaired by Dr. Isher Judge Ahluwalia, the estimates are worked out at 2009-10 prices using service benchmarks developed by MOUD. The catalog supports planning and policy analysis for urban transport investment needs and prioritization of infrastructure spending by decision-makers.",
  "generated_sector": "Infrastructure; Roads"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Estimates of components nutritional status of children aged 7 months-60 months compare ICDS beneficiaries with non-ICDS beneficiaries across India. The catalog provides state-wise distribution across nutritional status grades (Normal and Grades 1 to 4) for ICDS children, alongside corresponding estimates for non-ICDS children. These indicators support assessment of child nutrition outcomes under the Integrated Child Development Scheme and help inform program planning and evaluation by NITI Aayog.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together estimates on components of health check-up and selected related indicators, covering measures such as child health at birth, early initiation of breastfeeding, diarrhoea status, and household practices like use of iodised salt and boiling water during illness. It also includes awareness-related indicators linked to child development and health, including knowledge to delay or avoid pregnancy and measures to prevent anaemia. Published by NITI Aayog, the data supports monitoring and evaluation of health and nutrition programmes across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Estimates of Components of NHE-Child Index track the percentage of mothers who followed the advices given by AWWs on key components of child care. The indicators cover taking care and monitoring of a child’s growth, immunization, breast feeding and colostrum feeding, treatment of diarrhoea, preparation of nutritious food, child education, and cleanliness and hygiene. Published by NITI Aayog, the India-focused series supports monitoring and evaluation of child nutrition and early childhood development under ICDS-related interventions.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Egg production estimates for India provide State/UT-wise information on egg output along with related production parameters such as estimated number of layers and average yield per year. The coverage supports analysis of trends over time and comparisons across regions for egg production from fowls and ducks. Published by the Department of Animal Husbandry and Dairying under the Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying, the data is useful for planning, monitoring and policy work in the dairy and animal husbandry sector.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Dairying"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Estimates of Milk Production by Exotic/Crossbred Cows provide India-wide information on milk output from exotic/crossbred cows, along with supporting indicators such as number of animals in milk and average yield per animal. The series supports state/UT-wise analysis of dairy productivity and helps stakeholders monitor trends in cow-based milk production. Published by the Department of Animal Husbandry and Dairying under the Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying, it is useful for planning, performance assessment, and policy and program decision-making in dairying.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Dairying"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides year-wise estimates of egg production and per capita availability of eggs for India. It supports analysis of poultry and egg supply trends, helping stakeholders assess availability for consumption and plan development in the livestock sector. Data can be used for monitoring growth in poultry activities and for informing policy and program decisions related to egg production and nutrition-related availability. The estimates are published by the Department of Animal Husbandry and Dairying under the Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Dairying"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Year-wise estimates on milk production and per capita availability for India support planning and monitoring of the dairy sector. The indicators help assess supply trends, availability for consumption, and demand-supply balance for policymakers and researchers. Published by the Department of Animal Husbandry and Dairying and the Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying, the catalog focuses on dairy outputs and consumption availability at the national level.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Dairying"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Estimates of Wastelands in India compile area estimates for non-forest degraded land and forest degraded area, including saline and alkaline lands, wind-eroded area, and water-eroded area. The catalog supports analysis of land degradation patterns and monitoring of wasteland categories for planning and policy use. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, it provides India-wide coverage to support environment and land management decision-making.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Forest Resources"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides estimates of production, yield rates and the share of animals in meat production across India. It covers estimated numbers of slaughtered animals, average yield per animal, and meat production for cattle, buffalo, sheep, goat, pig and poultry. These indicators support planning and monitoring in animal husbandry and meat supply chains, including assessment of productivity and composition of meat output. The data are published by the Department of Animal Husbandry and Dairying and the Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Animal Husbandry"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Annual estimates on yield rates and the share of fowls and duck in egg production for India, covering DESI and improved varieties of fowls and ducks. The catalog provides indicators such as the average number of layers, average yield per year, and egg production, including totals and shares across categories like fowls, ducks, and others. These data support monitoring of poultry productivity and planning for egg supply and animal husbandry development. Published by the Department of Animal Husbandry and Dairying under the Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Animal Husbandry"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides estimates on milk production in India, covering yield rates and the share of cross breed, non-descript, buffalo, and goats. It includes indicators such as average animals in milk, average yield per day, and milk production for cows (exotic and non-descript), buffalo, and goats, along with percentage change in milk. These data support planning and monitoring of dairy and livestock development by the Department of Animal Husbandry and Dairying and the Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Animal Husbandry"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Estimates of yield rates and the share of ram/weather, ewe and lamb in wool production for India. The catalog brings together annual estimates covering wool production, sheep shorn, and average yield per season for ram/weather, ewes and lambs, supporting analysis of productivity and composition of wool output. It is useful for planning and monitoring the sheep wool value chain and for policy and program review by the Department of Animal Husbandry and Dairying and the Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry and Dairying.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Animal Husbandry"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together evaluations of the Rajiv Gandhi Grameen Vidyutikaran Yojana (RGGVY), a scheme aimed at rural electrification in India. It focuses on assessing progress toward electrifying villages and habitations and expanding electricity access to rural households, including free connections for Below Poverty Line (BPL) families. The evaluations support evidence-based review of scheme performance and outcomes under implementation since 2005, with NITI Aayog as the publishing ministry/department.",
  "generated_sector": "Infrastructure; Power"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together Census 1991 data on women’s marital patterns, covering ever married women by age at marriage, currently married women by age at marriage, and duration of marriage. It supports analysis of marriage timing and marital duration alongside population breakdowns for Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India, the resources are useful for demographic research and policy planning focused on women and social groups across India and States.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together Census 2001 information on ever married women and their children, covering children ever born, male children ever born, and surviving children by sex. It supports analysis of fertility and child survival patterns among ever married women, including breakdowns for male and female surviving children. Published by the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India under the Ministry of Home Affairs/Department of Home, the scope covers India and its states for Census 2001.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog presents Census 2001 statistics on ever married and currently married population by age at marriage, duration of marriage, and educational level. It distinguishes between ever married and currently married persons, supporting analysis of marital patterns alongside education and time since marriage. The data are intended for demographic research, policy planning, and studies on marriage-related life-course transitions. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs; Department of Home, through the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India, for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog presents Census 2001 data on ever married and currently married population by age at marriage, duration of marriage, and religious community. It distinguishes between ever married persons and currently married persons, supporting analysis of marital patterns and transitions over the life course. The statistics are compiled for India and its States, enabling comparative studies of marriage timing and marital duration across religious communities. Published by the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India under the Ministry of Home Affairs.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides Census 2001 statistics for India on ever married and currently married population, broken down by age at marriage, duration of marriage, work status, and occupation. It supports analysis of how marital history relates to employment and occupational patterns across the population. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs, Department of Home, and the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India, the tables are designed for demographic research and planning that uses Census 2001 indicators.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides Census 1991 data on ever married and currently married women, broken down by present age, parity, and total children ever born by sex. It supports analysis of women’s marital status and fertility patterns, including variations across social categories such as Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes. Published by the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India under the Ministry of Home Affairs/Department of Home, the collection is intended for demographic research, policy planning, and census-based monitoring across India and its states.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides Census 1991 data on ever married and currently married women, broken down by present age and by surviving children and total surviving children, with results by sex. It supports analysis of women’s marital status patterns and child survival indicators, including disaggregation for Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes. Published by the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India under the Ministry of Home Affairs/Department of Home, the coverage is for India and States.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog presents Census 2001 statistics on ever married and currently married population in India, with breakdowns by age at marriage and duration of marriage. It distinguishes married, ever married, and currently married persons, including those in consensual and visiting partnerships, and supports analysis of marital patterns over time since marriage. Data are available with classifications including Scheduled Caste (SC) and Scheduled Tribe (ST). Published by the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India under the Ministry of Home Affairs/Department of Home.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together ex-legal case information for the City of Ahmedabad, Gujarat, covering the status of legal matters across different courts. It supports tracking case progress and understanding court-wise outcomes for stakeholders such as citizens, legal practitioners, and urban governance teams. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs as part of the Smart Cities Mission, the resources focus on Ahmedabad and are oriented to urban service and administration use cases.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Grievances"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers ex-visitors counts at zoo complexes in Ahmedabad, Gujarat, including visitor statistics for the zoo, Bal Vatika, and the butterfly park. It supports monitoring of public engagement with urban recreation and biodiversity-themed facilities, and can be used for planning visitor management, staffing, and facility improvements. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, the focus is on city-level usage patterns for Ahmedabad’s zoo complex attractions.",
  "generated_sector": "Urban; Development"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides exchange rate data for the rupee vis-a-vis selected currencies of the world, supporting analysis of currency movements and their implications for prices and economic planning. It covers key bilateral rates against major currencies including US Dollar, Pound Sterling, Euro, Yen, Canadian Dollar and Brazilian Dollar. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the resources are useful for researchers, analysts and policymakers tracking exchange-rate trends for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers department-wise expenditure incurred on pay and allowances for civilian employees across central ministries and departments. It supports analysis of government spending patterns related to employee compensation, including pay and allowance components, for budgeting, monitoring, and policy review. Published by the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, the datasets provide India-wide coverage and are useful for researchers and administrators studying public employment costs and administrative expenditure trends.",
  "generated_sector": "Labour and Employment; Statistics"
}

